MAMUT-routing third-party and data-license notice
================================================

MAMUT-routing is a mixed software and benchmark project. The source code is MIT-licensed unless a file says otherwise. Benchmark data and generated artifacts are licensed at the benchmark-family level. Each family lives in its own repository, mounted here at benchmarks/<Family>, and carries its own LICENSE and NOTICE files, which prevail for that family.

Component licensing
-------------------

- Source code in this repository: MIT License.
- benchmarks/Sintef2008 (VRPTW): MAMUT-routing curation artifacts are provided under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the relevant rights. The underlying classical VRPTW benchmark definitions originate from Solomon (1987), Gehring and Homberger (1999), and the SINTEF VRPTW benchmark convention.
- benchmarks/Dimacs2021 (VRPTW): MAMUT-routing curation artifacts are provided under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the relevant rights. The benchmark contract follows the 12th DIMACS Implementation Challenge VRPTW rules.
- benchmarks/Ortec2022 (VRPTW): ORTEC instances and related redistributed BKS files are provided under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0).
- benchmarks/Dabia2013 (TDVRPTW and TDVRP): MAMUT-routing curation artifacts are provided under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the relevant rights. The underlying Solomon-derived IGP instances are those distributed with the MIT-licensed open-source solver of Lera-Romero, Miranda Bront and Soulignac (2020).
- benchmarks/Ari2018 (TDVRPTW and TDVRP): MAMUT-routing curation artifacts are provided under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the relevant rights. The underlying benchmark definitions originate from the time-dependent TSPTW generator of the Arigliano et al. lineage.
- benchmarks/Vu2020 (TDVRPTW and TDVRP): MAMUT-routing curation artifacts are provided under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the relevant rights. The underlying raw files originate from the Vu et al. (2020) time-dependent TSPTW benchmark material.
- benchmarks/Rifki2020 (TDVRPTW and TDVRP): MAMUT-routing curation artifacts are provided under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the relevant rights. The underlying stepwise travel-time construction follows Rifki et al. (2020). Coordinates are a deterministic MAMUT-routing embedding.
- benchmarks/Lera2026 (TDVRPTW and TDVRP): MAMUT-routing generation and curation artifacts are provided under MIT where MAMUT-routing holds the relevant rights. The base data are the Gehring and Homberger (1999) instances as curated in benchmarks/Sintef2008, with IGP (Ichoua-Gendreau-Potvin 2003) travel speeds.
- benchmarks/Blauth2024 (TDVRPTW): the instances, sidecars and best-known-solution files are provided under Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0). They are a value-exact conversion of the delivery-only instances of the vrptdt-benchmark of Blauth et al. (2024), which carries the same licence because it incorporates Uber Movement speed data.
- benchmarks/Poryos2026 (CVRP, VRPTW, TDVRP and TDVRPTW layers): OSM-derived benchmark instances, sidecars, generated route artifacts, and related benchmark data are distributed under ODbL 1.0 where they derive from OpenStreetMap data.
- benchmarks/Mamut2026 (CVRP): OSM-derived benchmark instances, sidecars, generated route artifacts, and related benchmark data are distributed under ODbL 1.0 where they derive from OpenStreetMap data.

